{Color gamut is defined as the range of colors that a particular device can produce or record.}
{It is usually shown by an enclosed area of the primary colors of the device on the chromaticity diagram.}
{The most commonly known color gamut might be “NTSC” (established in 1953 by the US FCC), however, it is not a standard color gamut.}
{“sRGB” is the standard color gamut established by the IEC in 1999.}
{The reason for standardizing a color gamut was to promote an easier way for color reproduction.}
